{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgNCtjRncENmNYArNz3U5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UHQ8D2VKUrMPDwdaocW8LF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -I - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json, subprocess, sys\nPY=\"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13\"\nCLI=[PY,\"-B\",\"/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py\",\n \"--policy\",\"/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/review-operator/claude-expectation-continuation-1/reviewer-policy.json\",\n \"--policy-sha256\",\"35a090513986c0bc1cd57cb13987979b055ff9afccc1bc49952d2376643631ab\",\n \"--principal\",\"reviewer\",\"call\",\"--request\",\"-\"]\nCWD=\"/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills\"\ndef call(req):\n    p=subprocess.run(CLI,input=json.dumps(req).encode(\"utf8\"),capture_output=True,cwd=CWD)\n    out=p.stdout.decode(\"utf8\",\"replace\")\n    try:\n        return json.loads(out)\n    except Exception:\n        print(\"NONJSON rc\",p.returncode); print(out[:3000]); print(p.stderr.decode(\"utf8\",\"replace\")[:3000]); sys.exit(1)\ndef strip(o):\n    if isinstance(o,dict): return {k:(\"<b64 %d bytes>\"%len(v) if k==\"content_base64\" else strip(v)) for k,v in o.items()}\n    if isinstance(o,list): return [strip(x) for x in o]\n    return o\n\nTEXT=\"\"\"Reviewer expectations recorded before candidate exposure by urn:stdo-skills:T001:claude:reviewer:1 (anthropic-claude), continuing the timed-out source-only session under the same declared identity. No candidate assessment is made here.\n\nORACLE. USER-OUTCOME.md and the eight selected STDO 3.0.1 method and a_c clauses acquired under OperationEvidence sha256:cdd9ae5b2b78e83285dd9ab22a0d09727bd24351a73c2bf1f0ca76f4f5e99157: EVALUATION section 3 (independent assessment), EXECUTIVE_BASELINE section 10 (Reviewer frame), ACTIVATION construction availability/disposition and transition evidence, SPEC_METHOD section 11 (build-tenant binding), AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS section 5 (traversals and functor kinds), a_c PRODUCT F_D support/method ownership/qualification boundary, REQ-AC-FD-005 to 013. Not oracle: candidate bytes, the candidate's own specification clauses, prior review verdicts or constructor summaries in the proof sources, test totals, package presence.\n\nEXPOSURE. No candidate population bytes were acquired through native tools. Seen before this record: CLAIM.json and SELECTION.json coordinates (paths, sha256, authors, component scopes); tools.describe output of the running a_c CLI (operations list, content schemas, method_profile id and sha, builder uri, unsupported list), which is runtime behaviour of the native301 candidate tool rather than its source; host bootstrap loaded before activation (apps-root and repository-root CLAUDE.md, a git status naming modified a_c tool paths and an untracked stdo_skills/ directory, a memory index). The repository-root CLAUDE.md carries one paragraph describing stdo_skills. No product-root file was read. The tool reports external_exposure unknown and semantic independence not certified; this record certifies neither.\n\nA. common-what (shared WHAT, bootstrap and ownership surfaces). Falsified if any relation below is violated.\nA1 Basis: exactly one immutable released STDO 3.0.1 identity with exact digest is the static methodology basis, and method law is routed to it rather than restated. A mutable sibling checkout, a bare version label, or duplicated method clauses falsify.\nA2 Ownership: the shared WHAT states skill obligations and defers lifecycle, roles, triage and re-entry, activation, result algebra, review and independence, and acceptance semantics to their 3.0.1 owners by reference. A second lifecycle, new result values, or ceremony stronger than the selected release falsify.\nA3 One WHAT, two independent HOW tenants: requirements are host-neutral; the codex and claude tenants are located by a registry and own their bindings; host-specific tuning lives in tenant design and realisation. Host-specific packaging stated as WHAT, or one tenant depending on or governing the other, falsifies.\nA4 Decoupling: a lifecycle separate from the release-matched cohort, with no live claim of cohort membership, RC formalisation, remote publication, general benefit or complete methodological qualification.\nA5 Construction versus acceptance: no live surface or ticket presents constructor self-review, Root selection or tool output as acceptance; tenant-local truth stays derivative until ratified in specification; acceptance is an owner decision with its own record.\nA6 Traceability: each shared requirement grounds in the user outcome (harmonise the tools with 3.0.1; two tenants; same requirements, different tenants; decoupled dogfood; executive build with current tooling) or in a named 3.0.1 owner clause; scenarios exercise the outcome, not counts.\n\nB. native301-auth-increment (a_c method binding and credential routing). Falsified if any relation below is violated.\nB1 Exact binding: the consumer's operative method profile (3.0.1) is a caller-supplied input bound by exact identity and digest, separate from the builder (v2.5.1-rc.2) and from represented subject versions; no implicit latest adoption; label equality, file presence or co-location compose no binding.\nB2 Credential routing: policy and principal are explicit digest-bound inputs; preflight reports missing or mismatched support before any effect; a shape check, role name, principal label or invocation mints no admission or work authority; credential sources are declared dependencies, not undeclared environment, filesystem or global reads.\nB3 Failure contracts: every stop or refusal maps to exactly one core value, never satisfied; refusals retain cause and evaluated predicate; timeout, cancel and interruption keep unknown-effect semantics; an operation_outcome of satisfied means output availability only.\nB4 F_D scope: F_D is claimed only for operations with a declared closed domain, exact basis, dependency closure and termination argument; no whole-a_c or blanket F_D claim; results.conjoin is declared unsupported, not silently emulated; the deterministic wrapper does not make F_P output deterministic or semantic evidence of success.\nB5 Evaluation-operation profile: review and evidence paths preserve the judged subject, write only their own protected evidence, record acquisitions and exposure, and support expectation recording before exposure. Writes into source or candidate trees, or silent replacement of an expectation artifact, falsify.\nB6 Proof: the environment-passthrough, native301 and conjunction tests are inside the manifold; each proves only the relation it names; a passing total is not qualification; a durable binding or credential claim is not established solely by same-process proof.\nB7 Examples and README describe the supported ordinary call path consistently with B1 to B5; an example that uses an undeclared path or asserts authority the contracts deny falsifies.\n\nC. codex-tenant-static-merits (observed post-timeout package from worker:2 with no closed return). Falsified if any relation below is violated.\nC1 Binding declared: the tenant design declares its calculus binding (requirements calculus to skill instructions and tool operations) and execution binding (the Codex skill host) with the exact 3.0.1 basis; the inventory locates the tenant and is not the binding.\nC2 Routing, not duplication: SKILL and references route the actor to exact 3.0.1 clauses and a_c contracts; paraphrase is marked as routing; no rival method law, task ledger or decision authority.\nC3 Useful behaviour: guidance on basis, delegation, qualification, recovery and release-install preserves verdict versus recommendation versus disposition, construction availability versus assessment, unperformed equals no result, and independence by authorship rather than role name or fresh context. Instructions to self-accept, to treat passing checks as acceptance, or to assess one's own authorship falsify.\nC4 Tool use: tool guidance invokes declared a_c operations with explicit policy, principal and request envelope; it names no unsupported operation (results.conjoin) and does not present tool output as semantic acceptance.\nC5 Proportionality: no ceremony stronger than 3.0.1; a small Executive context with visible late acquisition; whole-corpus loading or universal review rounds falsify.\nC6 Packaging: the package verifier and README claim structure and syntax only; host discovery, automatic triggering, Q01-Q12 host trials, efficiency and acceptance are recorded open, never implied by a pass.\nC7 Standing: tenant surfaces present no closed return or accepted status; incomplete availability concerns the construction output, not the subject's fitness.\n\nCROSS-CUTTING. X1 Authorship from frozen custody is openai-codex for all three components; adopted Claude-authored text found in any component limits this Reviewer's independence for that part and is reported, not repaired. Proof sources (assessment, custody and return files) are reusable factual and trial evidence, not judgment. X2 Result algebra per component: a violated supported relation is falsified; performed but insufficient assessment is indeterminate; an unusable basis is invalid_basis; unavailable capability is out_of_frame; unperformed is not_performed with no invented result. Findings S0-S4 bind file:line, violated relation, reachable evidence and consequence, with cause separated from inference and no repair authored. X3 Open by construction: host Q01-Q12 trials, automatic discovery, efficiency or benefit, and acceptance are not expected from this population and will not be scored pass or fail.\"\"\"\n\ntask=call({\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\",\"id\":\"claude-expectation-continuation-task-read\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"arguments\":{\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"root\":\"review\",\"path\":\"claude-expectation-continuation-1/TASK.md\",\"object\":None,\"sha256\":\"41cde964929df7d0be982e815a50f234e20e9f52f0d112d71da1bb5d55f96d19\",\"selector\":None},\"encoding\":\"utf8\"}})\nif task.get(\"status\")!=\"ok\":\n    print(\"TASK READ FAILED\"); print(json.dumps(strip(task))[:4000]); sys.exit(1)\ncontent=task[\"result\"][\"value\"][\"content\"]\ni=content.find('{\\n  \"schema\"')\ntpl,_=json.JSONDecoder().raw_decode(content[i:])\nargs=tpl[\"arguments\"]; si=args[\"expectation_body\"][\"source_inputs\"]\nassert tpl[\"operation\"]==\"review.prepare\" and args[\"phase\"]==\"expectation\" and args[\"sources\"]==[] and args[\"proof\"]==[] and args[\"expectations\"] is None and len(si)==9, \"template shape\"\nassert \"REPLACE WITH\" in args[\"expectation_body\"][\"text\"], \"placeholder\"\nprint(\"TEMPLATE id:\",tpl[\"id\"],\" source_inputs:\",[x[\"id\"][7:19] for x in si])\nargs[\"expectation_body\"][\"text\"]=TEXT\nresp=call(tpl)\nprint(\"\\n=== RECORD RESPONSE (content_base64 stripped) ===\")\nprint(json.dumps(strip(resp))[:14000])\nev=resp.get(\"evidence\")\nif resp.get(\"status\")==\"ok\" and ev:\n    er=call({\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\",\"id\":\"claude-expectation-continuation-record-evidence\",\"operation\":\"evidence.read\",\"arguments\":{\"artifact\":ev}})\n    env=er.get(\"result\",{}).get(\"value\",{}).get(\"envelope\",{})\n    pl=env.get(\"payload\",{})\n    print(\"\\n=== RECORD EVIDENCE provenance.actor ===\");print(json.dumps(env.get(\"provenance\",{}).get(\"actor\")))\n    print(\"=== payload.artifacts ===\");print(json.dumps(pl.get(\"artifacts\")))\n    print(\"=== payload.acquisitions ===\");print(json.dumps(pl.get(\"acquisitions\")))\n    print(\"=== payload.gaps ===\");print(json.dumps(pl.get(\"gaps\")))\n    rwe=pl.get(\"response_without_evidence\",{}).get(\"result\",{})\n    print(\"=== result.artifact ===\");print(json.dumps(rwe.get(\"artifact\")))\n    v=rwe.get(\"value\",{}) if isinstance(rwe,dict) else {}\n    for k in (\"expectations\",\"exposure\",\"gaps\",\"independence\",\"limits\",\"phase\",\"population_complete\",\"source_first\",\"expectation\"):\n        if isinstance(v,dict) and k in v: print(\"=== value.%s ===\"%k, json.dumps(strip(v[k]))[:3000])\nPYEOF","description":"Read TASK template, record expectations via review.prepare, read resulting evidence","timeout":180000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":157642,"cache_read_input_tokens":2856,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":157642},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.4.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.8.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.12.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.16.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.20.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"system_changed","cache_missed_input_tokens":53214}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"628dfe7c-13d9-4c76-8146-64fd9787ee38","uuid":"85e6d798-3018-4283-be64-9ff043327928","timestamp":"2026-10-25T03:03:51.062Z","request_id":"req_011CgNCtjCPRyLmLRFNBjZ4G","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UHQ8D2VKUrMPDwdaocW8LF":{"command":"cd /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills && /opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.